1
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:18,460
I never dreamed before

2
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:21,300
I'm gonna knock the door

3
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,870
into the world of perfect free

4
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:26,970
(You ain't no lonely!)

5
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:29,810
You're gonna say I'm lying

6
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:32,540
I'm gonna get the chance

7
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:36,110
I thought a chance is far from me

8
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,280
(You ain't no lonely!)

9
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,190
I was made to hit in America

10
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:43,050
(I was made to hit in America)

11
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:48,960
I was made to hit in America

12
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,630
You are the sun, you are the star

13
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:54,630
(To me, forever)

14
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:58,340
You are the sun, you are the star

15
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:01,570
(To me, forever)

16
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:14,020
I was made to hit in America

17
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:16,860
I was made to hit in America

18
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:19,720
(I was made to hit in America)

19
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,530
I was made to hit in America

20
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:25,300
(I was made to hit in America)

21
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:33,170
I was made to hit in America

22
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:46,210
Belle Ame...It means
"beautiful spirit" in French.

23
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,740
Bugger off. Hit the road.

24
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:53,730
-Jim, give me that!
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

25
00:01:53,730 --> 00:01:55,160
-Hey! They're waiting for us.
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

26
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,160
-Why are you saying this now? Shit!
-But, that makes Dying Breed appealing.

27
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:02,830
-What shall we do? That's irresponsible.
Hey Jim! What are you filming!?
-On top of that, Matt is wild.

28
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:09,410
Like a river flowing,
inspiration always flows from my mind.

29
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:13,410
-Hey! Dancing, dancing...Party man...
-Oh! He's a funny guy.

30
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:17,710
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...

31
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:26,260
Sometimes, there comes a special day,
while they're on tour.

32
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:29,090
It's a beautiful scene.

33
00:02:29,090 --> 00:02:33,270
Tokyo...a city of noise
and chaos. Techno-city.

34
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:34,170
Come on!

35
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:36,700
They had a live here, as well.

36
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:39,190
In the evening, with the shining moon.

37
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:44,510
They met a boy. It was
a very special event.

38
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,530
"Fishing Hole"

39
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:30,260
A long time ago, a female office worker
quit her job for no good reason...

40
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:32,360
and started the
Grateful Sound Summer Special

41
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,260
with some music-lover friends.

42
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:39,360
It all started when she was blown away
by the Glastonbury Festival in England,

43
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:43,540
and wondered if fans couldn't put together
a pure rock festival here in Japan.

44
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:47,440
Grateful Sound started
from that simple motive.

45
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:54,210
Nowadays, it's the biggest
outdoor event in Japan.

46
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:56,780
Are you that office worker?

47
00:03:56,780 --> 00:04:02,220
No...She was my sister,
who died last year.

48
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:03,380
I see...

49
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:08,860
Sorry for being so blunt,
but I have to talk business.

50
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,060
Sure...

51
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:13,430
You're friends with a member
of Dying Breed, aren't you?

52
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,570
Huh?

53
00:04:14,570 --> 00:04:18,070
I heard that two of their members
were at your live performance.

54
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:19,400
Yeah...

55
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:24,740
Couldn't you get them, Dying Breed,
to come to the Grateful Sound event?

56
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:26,580
What?!

57
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:28,880
They just finished their
world tour and are off now.

58
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,580
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'”

59
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,580
They just finished their
world tour and are off now.

60
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:33,420
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'”

61
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:33,420
Yeah...I know that, but I'm asking...

62
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:33,940
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'"

63
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:33,940
Hm...

64
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:34,500
Hm...

65
00:04:36,910 --> 00:04:40,920
Nowadays, Grateful Sound seems
like just a money-making tool.

66
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:44,220
I feel like it's moving
in the wrong direction.

67
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:48,590
Ran, the Japanese producer,

68
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:52,930
is planning to push one of the bands on
his label-a boring band called Belle Ame

69
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:57,920
featuring a young actor
named Yoshito Morozumi.

70
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:03,270
You know, my sister was someone...

71
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:07,640
who thought that music could change
the world consciousness of people.

72
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:15,120
Ran and Leon Sykes' RJ label can
only produce "feel-good" pop tunes.

73
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:18,020
"Escapist" music that
says everything is all right

74
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,990
just paralyzes people's consciousness

75
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:22,290
and steals away their ability
to solve the problems

76
00:05:22,290 --> 00:05:24,060
that they face in their everyday lives.

77
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,120
Yeah...

78
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:31,230
Of course, it doesn't really matter

79
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:34,800
that there are so many "feel-good"
pop groups out there...

80
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:40,410
...but I don't want Grateful Sound
taken over by groups like those.

81
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:43,910
You say music has the power
to change the world?

82
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:49,710
Yes...At least Dying Breed does!

83
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,020
I like you, Aunty...

84
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:58,260
A-Aunty?!

85
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,760
I'll get in touch with Eddy right away.

86
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,260
You will?!

87
00:06:02,260 --> 00:06:05,600
That is, if you let us
perform at Grateful Sound.

88
00:06:08,770 --> 00:06:09,760
-Oh!
-Oh!

89
00:06:13,610 --> 00:06:17,950
Actually...After hearing
Mongolian Chop Squad's CD,

90
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:23,290
I brought up your name, at one time...

91
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:27,690
To replace Loud Crime City,
who suddenly broke up.

92
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:34,960
Of course, your quality doesn't even
touch that of the other pro bands...

93
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,570
Hmm...Hmph!

94
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:40,740
Considering your future
possibilities and low cost,

95
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:43,570
there were some who agreed with me.

96
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,410
Mm...

97
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:47,080
-But...
-Huh?

98
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,670
Ran overruled me.

99
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,920
I don't know the reason,
but in this industry,

100
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:56,080
if you get on the wrong side of Ran,

101
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,420
it could be difficult getting ahead.

102
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,510
That's why I want to do it.

103
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:09,520
With backup from you and Leon,
it won't be impossible.

104
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:15,270
I think he said he'd stop by in two weeks,
on his way back from Australia...

105
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,780
I've decided! I'm going to
negotiate with Leon Sykes.

106
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:23,280
I hope you'll help us too, Aunty...

107
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,150
Aunty? My name is Kazuo Sato!

108
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,120
Wasn't it great?

109
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,290
Yeah. Eddy's so awesome!

110
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:36,120
What about Matt?

111
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,390
A little scary, I think.

112
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:39,890
And that boy who sang...Who is he?

113
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:42,230
I've never heard of Yukiko...

114
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:43,400
You too, Atsuko?

115
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:45,900
What? You're performing
at Grateful Sound?

116
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:49,740
Yeah, well...I'm getting together
with a new band called Belle Ame.

117
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:52,240
We plan to release an album this Fall.

118
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,640
-A singer?
-That's great!

119
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:59,410
-Umm...
-Let's see...
Let's get something to eat.

120
00:07:59,410 --> 00:08:01,850
Oh...I pass.

121
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:04,650
Huh? What a wet blanket...

122
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,640
I'm kinda worried
about Ryusuke-kun's injuries.

123
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,930
Ah...I was just watching a movie...

124
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,090
So long!

125
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:15,100
What, from now?

126
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:19,530
Maho...Eguchi-san,
Yohei Takami and Chiemi Kuniyoshi

127
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:20,770
are at that place I told you about.

128
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:28,610
Oh? They have a terrific salad there. Oh...
I think Koyuki likes Chiemi Kuniyoshi...

129
00:08:28,610 --> 00:08:30,950
I have all her CDs. I'm her biggest fan!

130
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:33,950
Oh, didn't you say you were
worried about Ryusuke's injuries?

131
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,120
He just needs to put some spit on them!

132
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:40,710
Um...Sorry, but no outsiders...

133
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:45,920
Oh...Then...

134
00:08:49,230 --> 00:08:51,060
Tell Ryusuke I said "Hi."

135
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,100
Well, it'll all work out.

136
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,600
Listen, how can you be so sure?

137
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,500
I dunno.

138
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:35,110
Can't you give us a good explanation?!

139
00:09:35,110 --> 00:09:38,370
When you're hungry,
you get snippy, don't you?!

140
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:44,720
You wanted to meet
Chiemi Kuniyoshi so much?

141
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:47,690
Yeah...I don't think
I'll be able to sleep tonight.

142
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:56,560
I...

143
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,230
I had a dream once...

144
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:09,080
There was a wide open space
that seemed to be veiled by mist,

145
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,840
and there was lots of trash...

146
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:17,750
Hot!! Damn you!
Are you trying to kill me?!

147
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,920
That trash...They were
picking it up, right?

148
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:24,090
The spirits of dead rockers...

149
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:26,090
-Huh?
-Huh?

150
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:29,930
"We're cleaning up after
your concert," they said.

151
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:34,290
Sid was doing it like he
didn't really want to, right?

152
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:41,210
A-After I saw that dream,
my fever had gone down and...

153
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,880
I don't know how they feel about it,

154
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:51,840
but there are bands that are
born from miraculous encounters.

155
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:55,210
Not anyone would do.

156
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:58,090
They're the only ones who could do it.

157
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:14,410
Hey, wait a minute!
I never saw a dream like that!

158
00:11:14,410 --> 00:11:20,580
I-I always dream in panoramic,
full-color, 3-D.

159
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:26,750
I haven't seen any dream that foretells
our performance at Grateful Sound!

160
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:31,530
Uh, Chiba-kun, it's just a dream...

161
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:35,100
But! I'm the only one
who didn't have that dream...

162
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,930
Chiba-kun, your noodles are getting mushy.

163
00:11:36,930 --> 00:11:38,700
Shut up, will you!

164
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:41,270
So was that dream
in black and white? Color?

165
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:43,640
Hm...I wonder...

166
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:45,940
Probably color.

167
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:48,200
What the heck...Aw, forget it!

168
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,630
Huh?

169
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:28,180
What is it? Someone fooling around?

170
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,160
Ouch!

171
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:43,660
Yo!

172
00:12:45,770 --> 00:12:48,600
Oh...I'm so sorry!

173
00:12:50,610 --> 00:12:52,640
You've gotta be quiet,
or you'll wake my mother.

174
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:53,630
Yeah...

175
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,450
You're okay now, Ryusuke-kun?

176
00:12:57,450 --> 00:12:59,110
Yeah, well...

177
00:12:59,110 --> 00:13:02,780
Why'd you two drop in like this?

178
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:08,120
Well...I wanted to see
your surprised face!

179
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:08,960
Here!

180
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:11,360
Huh? What is it?

181
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,790
"Kuniyoshi"

182
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:13,360
"Kuniyoshi"

183
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:13,360
It's the real thing.

184
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,350
It's the real thing.

185
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:20,630
This...Could this be?

186
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,940
It's Chiemi Kuniyoshi's autograph.

187
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,100
Wow!

188
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,480
Hey...Your folks are gonna get up.

189
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,670
W-What's she like?

190
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:36,420
Mm...Well...A nice girl,
like she is on television.

191
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:37,590
Ah...

192
00:13:37,590 --> 00:13:39,610
She said to tell you "Hi."

193
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:45,430
I'm going to treasure it.
Thanks a lot, Maho.

194
00:13:45,430 --> 00:13:46,420
Hm?

195
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:57,230
"The moment the scent...
of excitement explodes..."

196
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:57,230
Boy, you've really grown up, haven't you?

197
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:00,610
Stupid brother...

198
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:05,110
Koyuki...Why was this magazine
by your pillow?

199
00:14:05,110 --> 00:14:06,240
No reason...

200
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:09,420
Oh...I'm beat.

201
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:15,460
Koyuki, can I stay overnight?

202
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:18,630
Huh? But I've got only one bed.

203
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:23,300
Well, y'see...Ryusuke's bedding stinks
and it's full of lice.

204
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,200
Shut up.

205
00:14:25,730 --> 00:14:27,220
Besides, Ryusuke's here too.

206
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:34,170
No. I'm going home. I can't
sleep in a strange bed.

207
00:14:38,650 --> 00:14:41,050
Okay, well...Take care of her.

208
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,310
Ray!

209
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:49,420
Ouch...Listen, I'm injured, you know...

210
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:50,860
Take care...

211
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:53,550
See ya later.

212
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:56,890
Be careful...

213
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,110
Say, do you have something
I can change into?

214
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:12,880
Uh, just a minute...

215
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:27,960
I...I'm going to do some composing...

216
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:30,960
Okay. Well, good night.

217
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:26,280
Koyuki? Come over here,
if you're going to sleep.

218
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,650
Huh?

219
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:36,950
'Kay...

220
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:56,920
Koyuki...

221
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:59,420
-Koyuki...
-Huh?

222
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:03,620
You really looked great
in that movie, Koyuki.

223
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:11,300
Truly...You looked really great.

224
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,120
Thanks...

225
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,280
You know...

226
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:33,290
We kissed that day...
What did that mean?

227
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:37,820
Or, what do I mean to you?
Maho...Are you asleep?

228
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:28,530
"Thank you, Koyuki.
6:30 a.m. I'm going home. Maho"

229
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:42,210
You really looked great
in that movie, Koyuki.

230
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:47,560
Mm...Good morning...

231
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,830
Good morning.

232
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:49,960
Good morning.

233
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:54,060
-What?!
-Quit dawdling, will you?

234
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:57,910
Hurry up and wash your face and eat.

235
00:18:57,910 --> 00:18:59,570
Y-Yeah...

236
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:02,740
Maho-chan...
Please help yourself to seconds.

237
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,910
Thank you.

238
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:09,080
My mother, that night, was really scary.

239
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:12,590
Listen to me! When a man is going
to act like a full-fledged man...

240
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:15,760
-he has to be able
to take full responsibility...
-Yes, ma'am...

241
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:16,950
Yes...

242
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,900
Hey, I don't see baldy
with golden teeth today.

243
00:19:40,210 --> 00:19:42,880
You showed up in front of me again...

244
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,370
You must be crazy.

245
00:19:46,550 --> 00:19:49,060
I brought the Beck's favorite today.

246
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,220
Hmph...

247
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:53,230
Beck is super shy
and gets so lonely easily.

248
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:55,230
Maybe because it came
from the way he looks.

249
00:19:55,230 --> 00:19:56,790
So take good care of him.

250
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:04,940
I heard the Mongolian Chop Squad made it
to the top 10 in the U.S. College charts.

251
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:07,240
Uh-huh...

252
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:10,610
You could say that's quite
a big hit for that kind of music.

253
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,080
I guess the movie worked.

254
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:16,520
If they weren't from some
minor Indies label from Chicago

255
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:18,640
they woulda done a lot better, I think.

256
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:22,920
Maybe you're right.

257
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,190
What do you want?!

258
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:28,430
Are you here for the dog food, or what?

259
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:30,860
It's the Grateful Sound...

260
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:41,170
What the fuck?!

261
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:52,880
Now, take your time!

262
00:20:54,390 --> 00:20:59,060
Concentrate! You can't be good
at anything unless you concentrate.

263
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,400
Yo! Tanaka-kun...

264
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,190
Oh, Kigata-kun...You're into wrestling?

265
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:07,740
Well, I have my eye on the Olympics.

266
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:09,900
That's impressive!

267
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:14,910
You and Hiromi-san get on well, don't you?

268
00:21:14,910 --> 00:21:16,540
Oh...we do?

269
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:26,320
Hm...I think she probably...
likes you.

270
00:21:29,590 --> 00:21:31,260
That's not...

271
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:32,380
Excuse me...

272
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:36,930
I saw the movie...
Can I have your autograph?

273
00:21:36,930 --> 00:21:38,760
-Ee...Aah...
-Who, me?!

274
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:41,830
Koyuki-kun!

275
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:45,430
Hiromi-chan...

276
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:52,780
I saw it! The movie...

277
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:55,450
I went to see it yesterday, with a friend.

278
00:21:55,450 --> 00:21:57,280
Really?

279
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:59,450
I was so impressed!

280
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:01,820
You were so big on screen.

281
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:06,430
The kids in the class
are all talking about you.

282
00:22:06,430 --> 00:22:08,130
Oh?

283
00:22:08,130 --> 00:22:12,660
I wanted to tell you that, so I came
running in my leotard-so embarrassing...

284
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,830
T-Thanks...

285
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,440
Bye!

286
00:22:28,150 --> 00:22:32,650
I still have a lot to learn...

287
00:22:32,650 --> 00:22:36,650
but I'll be happy if the movie
does some good for Beck...

288
00:22:38,930 --> 00:22:41,660
Then...summer will come.

289
00:22:50,210 --> 00:22:52,310
Another minute

290
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:55,010
Feelin' so fine

291
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,550
You turn the freeze

292
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:02,280
into warm light

293
00:23:04,390 --> 00:23:07,860
Had a premonition

294
00:23:07,860 --> 00:23:10,530
I've been waitin' ever since

295
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:14,040
My world comin' down

296
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:16,830
It's got me spinnin' 'round

297
00:23:18,610 --> 00:23:24,780
If you really wanna fly

298
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:27,540
you gotta let go

299
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:42,130
Simply the most

300
00:23:42,130 --> 00:23:44,170
big sensation

301
00:23:44,170 --> 00:23:46,970
(once you're here you won't go back)

302
00:23:46,970 --> 00:23:49,240
She's really pretty

303
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:51,240
One-eyed vision

304
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:54,080
(lose the fear it don't come back)

305
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:57,580
Little sister showed me

306
00:23:57,580 --> 00:24:00,250
Really took me for a ride

307
00:24:00,250 --> 00:24:01,920
My world comin' down

308
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:05,250
(once you're here you won't go back)

309
00:24:05,250 --> 00:24:09,280
(lose the fear it don't come back)

310
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:17,000
Next week, Page will
shoot beams from his eyes.

311
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,020
-Next week! Watch it!
-Write Music. Are you serious?!
